  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps`: a `WireU` / `WireV` stated before (or on) a section's first positioning move was cleared by `onRapid`, so the post wrote `G40 G00`, `T91`, the `C` word and `G01` as if the wire stood upright (the gap the last Codex run reported on #1497). That lean is now refused by name (\"a leaning positioning move (upper guide offset)\") and the whole section is neither threaded nor cut. The next section posts as before.\n- The 4-axis refusal (no G74 / G75, no U V) **stays**, which the issue's \"Done means\" allows. `docs/decisions/1497-sodick-four-axis.md` records what the public Sodick manual confirms and what it leaves open. The manual (1998, Mark 21 / EX21) gives U V as offsets from X Y. For 4-axis, X Y lie on the part's bottom plane, and Table To Program / Table To Next are heights measured from the worktable. The \"absolute mode\" half of the U V sentence is not explained, and the manual gives no G74 example. Camcraft's stream carries the lower guide's X Y and the upper guide's offset. Neither the machine file nor the stream states the worktable height, so the guide-plane values cannot be converted to Sodick's planes from stated values. Writing them unconverted would post a wrong 4-axis cut.\n- The `sodick_alc400g::a_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights` failure that stopped the two Codex runs is **fixed on main** (PR #1857, commit 0e1f3709). It passes on `ce59ef446`, and the whole `sodick_alc400g` suite passes in this PR's quick gate.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew `crates/post/tests/sodick_four_axis.rs` (5 tests, synthetic CNC streams):\n- `sodick_refuses_a_lean_before_the_first_rapid_and_threads_nothing`: the lean is stated on the rapid and before the section. The test checks the named warning and that no T91, C110, G01, G00 or T90 is written. **It fails on main's post.**\n- `sodick_lean_refusal_resets_for_the_next_vertical_section`: one warning, and the next section posts whole, once. **It fails on main's post.**\n- `sodick_still_refuses_a_leaning_cut`, `sodick_still_refuses_a_four_axis_section_by_name`: existing refusals, now pinned.\n- `sodick_vertical_stream_posts_unchanged`: the whole program body of a plain section.\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green. It ran the post suites (including `script_sodick_wire`, `sodick_taper`, `sodick_comp` and the new suite) and the app suites (including `conformance`, `sodick_wire_post` and `sodick_alc400g`). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. No golden changed: `nc/sodick-wire/wire_slug_punch.nc` is byte-identical.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe post has not been run on a Sodick control. No G74 output exists to check.\n\nOverlap: none with #1921 (wire kerf widening does not touch `sodick-wire.cps`). #1499 (tank / flushing) also edits `sodick-wire.cps`, in other hunks. Its PR is branched from main, not stacked.\n\nChangelog: The Sodick wire post refuses, by name, a section that leans the wire (WireU / WireV) before its first cut, instead of threading and cutting it upright (#1497)\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1497\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
